      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall recount his worthies: they shall stumble in their walk; they shall make haste to the wall thereof, and the defense shall be prepared.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The gates of the rivers shall be opened, and the palace shall be dissolved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Huzzab shall be led away captive, she shall be brought up, and her maids shall lead ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
